proposed_comments.body:
Hiding the dialog can synchronously raise its closing path. The active-state flag must be cleared before that call so a lifecycle transition cannot observe the control as active while its editor is already being torn down. Clear the flag first, then hide the dialog.

```suggestion
            _isActive = false;
            shortcutDialog?.Hide();
```

The fixture needs to isolate only the configuration held by the repository shared with `HotkeyConflictIgnoreHelper`; replacing the process-wide static repository makes the helper retain a different instance. Add a handle for that existing instance's configuration so it can be replaced and restored without changing the shared repository identity. Apply this together with the related fixture suggestions below.

```suggestion
        private static readonly FieldInfo RepositoryField = typeof(SettingsRepository<GeneralSettings>).GetField("settingsRepository", BindingFlags.Static | BindingFlags.NonPublic);
        private static readonly FieldInfo SettingsConfigField = typeof(SettingsRepository<GeneralSettings>).GetField("settingsConfig", BindingFlags.Instance | BindingFlags.NonPublic);
```

`HotkeyConflictIgnoreHelper` captures the shared settings repository during type initialization. Store that same repository and its previous configuration so the fixture can isolate settings without replacing the process-wide repository identity.

```suggestion
        private static SettingsRepository<GeneralSettings> repository;
        private static GeneralSettings previousSettingsConfig;
```

Creating and publishing a replacement static repository after `HotkeyConflictIgnoreHelper` initializes splits the fixture from the helper, producing order-dependent behavior and leaking global test state. Initialize the helper first, retain its repository, and temporarily replace only that repository's settings configuration.

```suggestion
            // Reuse the helper's repository and replace only its settings for isolation.
            // No Settings app, settings files, IPC connection or visible window is needed.
            RuntimeHelpers.RunClassConstructor(typeof(HotkeyConflictIgnoreHelper).TypeHandle);
            repository = (SettingsRepository<GeneralSettings>)RepositoryField.GetValue(null);
            previousSettingsConfig = (GeneralSettings)SettingsConfigField.GetValue(repository);
            repository.SettingsConfig = new GeneralSettings();
```

The fixture signals readiness from the test application constructor. Capture the thread dispatcher before constructing that application so initialization cannot complete while `dispatcher` is still unset. This keeps cleanup deterministic if the test app immediately signals its ready task.

```suggestion
                            dispatcher = DispatcherQueue.GetForCurrentThread();
                            _ = new ShortcutTestApplication(ready);
```

Cleanup currently restores shared process state only after the UI-thread assertions succeed. A timeout or enqueue failure would leave the replacement settings configuration installed for later tests. Keep the UI shutdown assertions, but restore the shared configuration in `finally`.

```suggestion
            try
            {
                if (dispatcher != null)
                {
                    Assert.IsTrue(dispatcher.TryEnqueue(() => Application.Current.Exit()));
                    Assert.IsTrue(uiThread.Join(Timeout), "The test XAML thread did not exit.");
                }
            }
            finally
            {
                SettingsConfigField.SetValue(repository, previousSettingsConfig);
            }
```
